# Minimum distance to travel to cover all intervals
We can solve this problem by concentrating only on endpoints. Since the requirement is to cover all intervals by reaching a point, all intervals must a share a point for answer to exist. Even the interval with leftmost end point must overlap with the interval right most start point. First, we find right most start point and left most end point from all intervals.
